    {
      "id": "CARD-AM-05-concept",
      "conceptId": "C-AM-05",
      "kind": "concept",
      "title": {
        "en": "SSB and VSB compared with DSB-SC",
        "or": "DSB-SC ସହିତ SSB ଓ VSB ତୁଳନା"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "Amplitude-modulation variants differ in which spectral components they transmit. DSB-SC sends both sidebands, requiring bandwidth 2B for a message whose highest frequency is B. SSB sends only one sideband and ideally requires bandwidth B, making better use of a restricted channel. VSB sends one sideband with a small vestige of the other; its bandwidth lies between ideal SSB and full DSB for a comparable message. The vestige eases practical filtering near the carrier. These are spectrum choices, not separate message types. Our lab uses DSB-SC, so SSB and VSB implementation is outside the lab route, although their comparison belongs in this chapter.",
        "or": "Amplitude modulation ର ପ୍ରକାରଗୁଡ଼ିକ କେଉଁ Spectral component ପଠାଯାଏ ତାହାରେ ଭିନ୍ନ। Message ର ସର୍ବାଧିକ Frequency B ହେଲେ DSB-SC ପାଇଁ Bandwidth 2B। SSB କେବଳ ଗୋଟିଏ Sideband ପଠାଏ, ତେଣୁ ideal Bandwidth B। VSB ଗୋଟିଏ Sideband ସହିତ ଅନ୍ୟଟିର ଛୋଟ ଅଂଶ ପଠାଏ। ସମାନ Message ପାଇଁ ଏହାର Bandwidth SSB ଓ DSB ମଧ୍ୟରେ ରହେ। ଏହି ଛୋଟ ଅଂଶ Carrier ନିକଟରେ practical filtering କୁ ସହଜ କରେ। ଆମ lab DSB-SC ବ୍ୟବହାର କରେ; SSB/VSB ତୁଳନା chapter ରେ ଥିଲେ ମଧ୍ୟ lab ପୂର୍ବରୁ ଆବଶ୍ୟକ ନୁହେଁ।"
      },
